{"file_spec":1.2,"file_creator":"senbazuru material study","file_title":"Bird base folding sequence","file_description":"Start with the collapsed square base and lift the south-east corner into the first petal. Then fold the north-west corner on the underside into the second petal, keeping the first at its nearly closed inspection angle. Drag to view the underside during the second stage. The last state presses both petals flat to complete the bird base.","file_classes":["diagrams"],"file_frames":[{"edges_assignment":["B","B","B","B","B","B","B","B","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","V","V"],"edges_foldAngle":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,180,-180,-180,0,0,-180,-180,0,0,-180,-180,0,0,-180,-180,0,0,0,0],"edges_vertices":[[0,4],[4,1],[1,5],[5,2],[2,6],[6,3],[3,7],[7,0],[0,8],[8,2],[8,9],[9,4],[9,0],[9,1],[8,10],[10,5],[10,1],[10,2],[8,11],[11,6],[11,2],[11,3],[8,12],[12,7],[12,3],[12,0],[9,10],[11,12]],"faceOrders":[[0,1,-1],[3,2,-1],[4,2,-1],[4,3,1],[5,2,-1],[5,3,1],[5,4,-1],[6,0,1],[6,1,-1],[6,7,-1],[7,0,1],[7,1,-1],[8,9,1],[8,12,-1],[8,13,-1],[9,12,-1],[9,13,-1],[10,11,1],[10,12,-1],[10,13,-1],[11,12,-1],[11,13,-1],[14,8,-1],[14,9,1],[14,10,-1],[14,11,1],[14,12,-1],[15,8,-1],[15,9,1],[15,10,-1],[15,11,1],[15,13,-1]],"faces_vertices":[[0,4,9],[4,1,9],[1,5,10],[5,2,10],[2,6,11],[6,3,11],[3,7,12],[7,0,12],[0,8,12],[8,0,9],[8,2,11],[2,8,10],[8,9,10],[9,1,10],[8,11,12],[11,3,12]],"frame_attributes":["2D"],"frame_classes":["foldedForm"],"frame_description":"Traditional bird base with two lifted petal flaps. Adapted from examples/bird-base.cp: normalize to a unit square with y up, reorder vertices, add valley hinges 9-10 and 11-12, and leave the four outer midline segments flat. The inner axis points are 1 - 1/sqrt(2) from the centre. The old CP alone folds with all four corners together; these petal hinges lift SE and NW to the opposite tip. See examples/README.md for Oriedita's MIT provenance and the added construction. This endpoint does no